                <pb facs="1264" n="1114" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1114"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Wilson to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-03-24"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Wilson advises the department that he is in receipt of a note from the
                    foreign office giving information that the Belgian Government <pb facs="1265"
                        n="1115" xml:id="pg1115"/> “does not offer any objections to the Russian
                    proposition concerning the adhesion of nonsignatory powers to the convention of
                    1899, if this proposition receives the assent of all the signatory powers which
                    is required by article 60 of the said convention.”)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
